{"edits": [], "notes": "No edits proposed. The only listed finding (app/api_errors.py:10, @validator) is already fixed in the current content: @field_validator("username") is stacked on @classmethod, and the field_validator import is present.

The failing test is not caused by that finding. It comes from Pydantic v2 changing error message text. MESSAGE_CODES matches lowercase v1 strings ("field required", "value is not a valid integer") with str.startswith, but v2 produces "Field required" and "Input should be a valid integer, unable to parse string as an integer". So "username" falls through to INVALID and "age" falls through to INVALID. The test's "age": "old" case also depends on the v2 message text.

The fix would require changing MESSAGE_CODES (lines 20-22) and/or the matching in error_codes. Those lines are not covered by any listed finding, and the previous attempt to edit them was rejected as out of scope, so I did not retry it. A safe fix would be to match on the stable v2 error "type" field (err["type"]: "missing", "int_parsing", "string_too_short") instead of message text. That is a behavior-relevant change, so it should be reviewed and added as a new finding for app/api_errors.py before it is applied. Until then, tests.test_api_errors::test_codes will keep failing."}
